# Impossible OS user-mode test CROSS-TEST cleanup manifest
# ========================================================
#
# Deployed by `make userland` to C:\tests\usermode-cleanup.manifest.
# Read by the kernel-side launcher in
#   src/kernel/test/test_usermode.c -> u_cleanup_manifest_apply()
# AFTER the per-test scratch dir + Registry subkey teardown, so any
# entries listed here are wiped between every binary in addition to
# the automatic C:\Temp\utest\<name>\ + HKLM\SOFTWARE\ImpossibleOS\Test\<name>
# scrub that every binary gets automatically.
#
# When to add an entry:
#   - The test legitimately touches global state OUTSIDE its per-test
#     scratch dir (DLL cache, network sockets-on-disk, shared caches).
#   - A prior run's leftover could affect a later binary's assertions.
#
# When NOT to add an entry:
#   - State inside C:\Temp\utest\<name>\ -- already isolated.
#   - State inside HKLM\SOFTWARE\ImpossibleOS\Test\<name>\ -- already isolated.
#   - Files that live in the read-only sysroot (C:\hello.txt).
#
# Format: one absolute path per line. Two prefixes recognized:
#   C:\<path>       -- vfs_unlink / recursive tree delete
#   HKLM\<subkey>   -- RegDeleteTree under HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE
# `#` starts a line comment. Blank lines ignored.
#
# Example (disabled by default; uncomment when a test needs it):
# C:\Impossible\Temp\dll-cache
# HKLM\SOFTWARE\ImpossibleOS\NetworkState

# (no entries today -- the §9-§15 test binaries live inside their
# per-test scratch roots and don't need cross-test cleanup)
